>Hello All,
>I'd like to announce the creation of a new lustre-
>community at lists.lustre.org mailing list.  After discussions with the
>various Lustre parties in the community, we thought there should be a
>new list to focus the "meta" discussion related to Lustre development in
>the community, such as how feature design, code development, patch
>contribution, and landing is coordinated, and how to test the resulting
>code, test harnesses for simplifying this, the mechanics of code
>inspections, etc.
>
>We'd like to keep this high-level discussion separate from the technical
>and code-specific discussions on lustre-devel, and the usage questions
>and general discussion on lustre-discuss.
>
>I think we all agree that maintaining the quality of the Lustre codebase
>going forward is important to everyone, so I hope we can have a
>productive discussion.
>
>Cheers, Andreas
